From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maxim Stepanov <g.maxim.stepanoff@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 11:39:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(db): page query results server-side with header sorting
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wrappable single-SELECT queries now run through sql_paging::wrap with
LIMIT page_size+1 OFFSET page*page_size; the extra row detects further
pages without a count query. Header clicks in the results grid emit
SortRequested; QueryView stores the requested sort verbatim and re-runs
page 0, pushing sorted/merged rows back into the grid via set_result/
set_sort. Load more appends under the existing generation guard.
Table opens generate plain SELECT * FROM t — paging owns limits.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MQKuAnEREjToPLedE7KAqP
